error[SE0201]: `default` stands alone
  --> tests/err/outgroup.se:10:19
   |
10 |     output default, y() { out.y = 0.0; out.z = 0.0; }
   |                   ^ not alone
   = note: `output default(...)` writes every output no group names, so it lists none of its own (§8.3a)
   = help: write the named outputs as a group of their own

error[SE0201]: `derivative` does not take a list of names before its parameters
  --> tests/err/outgroup.se:19:16
   |
19 |     derivative x(u) { der.x = in.u; }
   |                ^ expected `(`
   = note: only `output` names what it writes, because only `out.` can be written in pieces: an output group is the feedthrough set of the outputs it lists (§8.3a)
